WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Rosa has a lump sum available and wants retirement payments to

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:08.680
begin next month. A single-premium immediate annuity uses one contribution to

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.500
establish income beginning within one year of purchase.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.840
Now change the facts: David places a lump sum into a

5
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.300
contract but plans income for ten years later.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.160
That is deferred income, even though he paid only once.

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.960
Immediate and deferred describe income timing.

8
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.520
Single and periodic describe how money goes into the contract.

9
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.000
Keep those classifications separate.

10
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:37.860
Also distinguish the beginning of payments from their duration.

11
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.180
An immediate annuity can provide a stated period or a lifetime

12
00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.480
pattern under its selected option.

13
00:00:45.498 --> 00:00:50.118
A single-premium deferred annuity starts with one contribution and postpones

14
00:00:50.118 --> 00:00:55.138
income. A flexible-premium deferred design permits contributions that

15
00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:56.798
vary within the contract's limits.

16
00:00:57.738 --> 00:01:01.598
A scheduled or fixed-installment design instead specifies a payment pattern.

17
00:01:02.298 --> 00:01:05.418
Do not confuse a fixed premium schedule with a fixed interest

18
00:01:05.418 --> 00:01:10.398
guarantee; one describes funding and the other describes the contract's

19
00:01:10.398 --> 00:01:14.618
credited return. David should check minimum payments, whether later

20
00:01:14.618 --> 00:01:18.958
contributions are accepted, and whether each new contribution begins its own

21
00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:23.698
surrender-charge period. Stopping contributions is not the same event as

22
00:01:23.698 --> 00:01:27.998
surrendering the contract. Existing value and available benefits must be

23
00:01:27.998 --> 00:01:29.758
evaluated under the issued provisions.

24
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.520
Assume David's annuity has a one hundred thousand dollar account value.

25
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.360
The question states that surrendering today incurs a five percent charge

26
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:45.084
on the entire amount, with no free allowance, market adjustment or

27
00:01:45.084 --> 00:01:49.691
other charge. The charge is five thousand dollars, leaving ninety-five

28
00:01:49.691 --> 00:01:52.064
thousand dollars before any tax.

29
00:01:52.764 --> 00:01:56.784
This is an insurer charge, not the federal additional tax on

30
00:01:56.784 --> 00:02:01.224
certain early distributions. Some contracts permit limited withdrawals

31
00:02:01.224 --> 00:02:06.164
without a surrender charge, but the percentage, timing and calculation base

32
00:02:06.164 --> 00:02:11.284
vary. An amount described as penalty-free by the insurer can still

33
00:02:11.284 --> 00:02:16.524
have tax consequences. Read which cost is waived before promising

34
00:02:16.524 --> 00:02:18.224
what David will actually keep.

35
00:02:19.086 --> 00:02:23.886
Nonforfeiture provisions preserve specified benefits when contributions stop

36
00:02:23.886 --> 00:02:26.106
or the owner exercises a permitted option.

37
00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:30.866
For contracts within Maryland's individual deferred-annuity law, the required

38
00:02:30.866 --> 00:02:35.126
provisions address paid-up annuity benefits and applicable surrender values.

39
00:02:35.986 --> 00:02:39.606
A paid-up deferred benefit uses the value already built to support

40
00:02:39.606 --> 00:02:42.106
a later benefit without further contributions.

41
00:02:43.126 --> 00:02:46.106
It is not automatically a refund of every premium on demand.

42
00:02:46.826 --> 00:02:51.846
Maryland's minimum calculation uses defined net considerations, interest and

43
00:02:51.846 --> 00:02:55.486
adjustments; it is not simply the current advertised rate applied to

44
00:02:55.486 --> 00:03:00.366
every deposit. The law also has scope exceptions, including variable and

45
00:03:00.366 --> 00:03:05.106
immediate annuities. Apply the correct contract category before importing a

46
00:03:05.106 --> 00:03:10.168
minimum-value rule. A bailout provision can allow withdrawal without the

47
00:03:10.168 --> 00:03:15.288
stated surrender charge if the insurer's renewal rate falls below a

48
00:03:15.288 --> 00:03:20.328
contract-defined level. Suppose the fictional provision sets

49
00:03:20.328 --> 00:03:24.096
a three percent threshold and the new credited rate is two

50
00:03:24.096 --> 00:03:25.328
and a half percent.

51
00:03:25.728 --> 00:03:29.908
The stated rate condition is met, but David must still follow

52
00:03:29.908 --> 00:03:31.728
the election window and other terms.

53
00:03:32.448 --> 00:03:36.808
A lower rate that remains above the threshold does not satisfy

54
00:03:36.808 --> 00:03:41.988
that example. Not every annuity has a bailout clause, and

55
00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:45.588
some designs use a rate cap rather than a credited interest

56
00:03:45.588 --> 00:03:50.708
rate. A contractual waiver does not erase federal income tax or

57
00:03:50.708 --> 00:03:54.868
every possible adjustment unless the applicable rule says so.

58
00:03:55.674 --> 00:04:01.054
Before income begins, a deferred contract may provide a death benefit

59
00:04:01.054 --> 00:04:06.454
based on account value, adjusted premiums or another stated guarantee.

60
00:04:07.174 --> 00:04:11.914
Suppose the contract promises the greater of eighty thousand dollars of

61
00:04:11.914 --> 00:04:17.154
eligible adjusted premiums or ninety thousand dollars of current account

62
00:04:17.154 --> 00:04:22.241
value. With no other adjustment, the stated benefit is ninety thousand

63
00:04:22.241 --> 00:04:27.414
dollars. That is not automatically income-tax-free life insurance proceeds

64
00:04:27.414 --> 00:04:30.314
merely because payment follows a death.

65
00:04:31.174 --> 00:04:35.914
After annuitization, the selected income option can produce a different

66
00:04:35.914 --> 00:04:41.214
outcome for survivors. Review the phase, the triggering person's death

67
00:04:41.794 --> 00:04:46.974
and the formula. Funding, surrender and death are separate

68
00:04:46.974 --> 00:04:50.314
events, so use the provision that matches the question.
